# Sai Health Hub — server environment variables
# Copy the names you need into Settings -> Environment variables.
# Never commit real values, and never put these in public/ frontend code.

# Optional: durable database (Phase 1). Free tier is enough.
# 1. Create a project at https://supabase.com (free).
# 2. Run scripts/supabase-schema.sql in the SQL editor.
# 3. Project Settings -> API: copy the Project URL and the service_role key.
# With both set, records survive redeploys. Without them the app uses local storage.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=

# Optional: higher AI limits (Phase 2). Without it the app uses a free keyless provider.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_MODEL=
